From: MedyMa maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] 1905: copy a validated SSID length as bytes

The parser already bounds SSIDs to 32 bytes and clears the 33-byte
destination. A byte copy preserves that length without strncpy truncation.

--- a/src/cmdu_tlv_parse.c
+++ b/src/cmdu_tlv_parse.c
@@ -1691,7 +1691,7 @@
 				if (os_strncmp(bss->ssid, ssid, ssid_len) ||
 					ssid_len != os_strlen(bss->ssid)) {
 					os_memset(bss->ssid, 0, sizeof(bss->ssid));
-					os_strncpy(bss->ssid, ssid, ssid_len);
+					os_memcpy(bss->ssid, ssid, ssid_len);
 				}
 			}
 		}
